    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1098">

                <pb facs="0799" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4178a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Letcher.</hi><anchor
                        n="91" xml:id="d1098-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This Department is desirous of learning the names and addresses of all American
                    citizens in Mexico who have not taken its advice to leave that country and
                    remain out until peace is restored therein. The information wanted is for the
                    Department’s guidance in any future action that it may be necessary to take, or
                    information that it may be necessary to give, respecting those citizens.</p>
                <p>You will, therefore, make public, through the newspapers within your jurisdiction
                    the following notice: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In order that the whereabouts of Americans remaining in Mexico may be
                            known and for the purpose of informing inquiring friends and relatives,
                            the Government of the United States of America has instructed the Consul
                            to ask all American citizens who for any reason do not deem it advisable
                            to leave Mexico at this time, to register their names and addresses
                            personally or by written communication, at this Consulate with the least
                            possible delay.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>After this notice shall have been repeatedly published for one week and the
                    registration of Americans shall have been completed, you will send to the
                    Department by mail copies of the publications containing the printed notices
                    inviting the registration and a list of the Americans who may have registered,
                    with their addresses. Whenever in your judgment there is doubt of the
                    notification so published reaching Americans in your district, you will make
                    free use of the telegraphs and mails and even messengers should the exigencies
                    of the case require.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1098-f1" n="91" type="source" xml:id="d1098-f1-content">
                <p>Same to Ciudad Juárez, Ciudad Porfirio Díaz, Matamoros, Monterey, Nuevo Laredo,
                    Vera Cruz, Durango, Hermosillo, Nogales and Tampico.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
